# reel's command line demo: a terminal screen in which reel checks and records a small code reel (demos/cli/hello.reel)
# of its own. `mise run demos cli` records it. The shell is real: the commands run, in a folder of their own, and the
# setup that gets there is cut with Hide … Show.
Import //demos/reel.reelpreset
Screen terminal

Output //docs/media/cli.mp4
Output //docs/media/cli.gif
Set WorkingDirectory //
Set Columns 84
Set Rows 20
Set FontSize 18
Set Title "hello — zsh"
Intro@crossfade,ease-out,600ms square ? "reel" "The command line too" : 2s
Outro@fade,800ms square ? "Recorded with reel" "brew install --cask mpdreamz/tap/reel" : 2s

Hide
Type@0ms "export PATH=$PWD/.build/debug:$PATH; rm -rf /tmp/hello; mkdir /tmp/hello; cp demos/cli/hello.reel demos/code/SpeechClock.swift /tmp/hello; cd /tmp/hello; clear"
Key return
Wait exit
Show
Say "Reel records the command line too: a real shell, in a terminal of its own."
Type "cat hello.reel"
Key return
Wait exit
Mark "Screen code" 1
Callout "Screen code" "a reel of a code screen"
Say "Here's a small reel. Check it before recording it,"
Callout off
Mark off
Type "reel check hello.reel"
Key return
Wait exit
Say "then record it."
Type "reel hello.reel"
Key return
Speed 4x
Wait /wrote .*hello.gif/
Wait exit
Speed off
Mark "hello.mp4" 2
Mark "hello.gif"
Say "Reel recording reel. And that's a take."
Sleep 1s
